At Kumano Nachi Taisha, "Taki-miya" (deity {{ill|Ōkuninushi|lt=Ōkuninushi-no-Mikoto|ja|大己貴命|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōkuninushi|ja_comment=jawiki redirects to 大国主}} (Takinawa Gongen), original Buddha Thousand-Armed Kannon) is considered the first pavilion, and the order descends one pavilion at a time, enshrining the eight deities of the Middle Four Shrines and the Lower Four Shrines in the sixth pavilion (Hassha-den), thus known as the "Thirteen Shrines Gongen".

